# Tree-construction cases that the SilkSurf html5ever TreeSink adapter does not
# yet reproduce. Each line records a known gap so a regression and a repair are
# both visible as a diff against this file; HTML5LIB_TREE_FAIL_ON_XPASS=1
# promotes a newly passing case to a hard failure.
#
# Two adapter shortcuts account for 199 of the 286 entries. Both need a DOM
# primitive that silksurf_dom::NodeKind lacks:
#
#   template (109) -- treesink.rs get_template_contents returns the template
#   element itself, so template content never reaches a separate fragment and
#   the children are dropped.
#
#   processing-instructions (90) -- treesink.rs create_pi renders a processing
#   instruction as a comment, because NodeKind carries no ProcessingInstruction
#   variant.
#
# The remainder are diffuse tree-construction gaps led by noscript01 (15,
# scripting-flag handling in the in-head-noscript insertion mode).

